{"type":"standard","title":"Jon Husted","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jon Husted</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q6270269","titles":{"canonical":"Jon_Husted","normalized":"Jon Husted","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jon Husted</span></span>"},"pageid":15724141,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Sen._Jon_Husted_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg/330px-Sen._Jon_Husted_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":412},"originalimage":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Sen._Jon_Husted_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg/3840px-Sen._Jon_Husted_official_portrait%2C_119th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":4130,"height":5162},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1381127695","tid":"f96f7321-cc40-11f1-a7e4-e8aa80cab6fb","timestamp":"2026-10-20T04:44:46Z","description":"American politician (born 1967)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Husted","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Husted?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Husted?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jon_Husted"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Husted","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Jon_Husted","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Husted?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jon_Husted"}},"extract":"Jon Allen Husted is an American politician serving since 2025 as the junior United States senator from Ohio. A member of the Republican Party, he served from 2019 to 2025 as the 66th lieutenant governor of Ohio and from 2011 to 2019 as the 50th Ohio secretary of state.","extract_html":"<p><b>Jon Allen Husted</b> is an American politician serving since 2025 as the junior United States senator from Ohio. A member of the Republican Party, he served from 2019 to 2025 as the 66th lieutenant governor of Ohio and from 2011 to 2019 as the 50th Ohio secretary of state.</p>"}